{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DR8jEMKdyfzeVBApJ185hM","type":"tool_result","content":"/bin/bash: /etc/bash.bashrc: Permission denied\nmetais render — Render the package's outputs from the inputs supplied, into a\ndirectory or to standard output.\n\nUsage:\n  metais render <package> --out <dir|-> [supply flags] [--only <path>]\n                [--overwrite] [--dry-run] [--now <time>]\n                [--sample [--optional <mode>] [--seed <n>] [--items <n>]]\n                [--json]\n\nThe package is opened and verified whole, and the inputs are supplied and\nvalidated, as metais inspect and metais validate do; an input that fails ends\nthe render with every finding of the inputs. Then every output is planned, an\nasset or a mirror as each file it writes, its path checked by the portable-path\nrules, and rendered in memory: every output is attempted, and each reports its\nfirst error. An asset is copied as it is, never rendered: its size counts\nagainst the output limits, and its bytes are read from the package as it is\nwritten. An output declaring newline: crlf then has its line endings made CR LF,\nand one naming a validate schema is parsed and validated against it, every\nfinding of every output reported. If any finding is an error, nothing is written\nanywhere. A container output is one zip of its entries, each rendered as an\noutput is, in the order its profile and its first entries give; its zip is\nwritten as it is assembled.\n\n--out is required, and names a directory. When it does not exist yet — the way\nto render — the outputs are written beneath a staging directory beside it,\n.metais-staging- followed by 16 hex digits, which is then renamed to it in one\nstep that never replaces anything: the directory either does not exist or holds\nevery output. Its missing parents are created.\n\nAn --out that exists must be a directory. One with no entry at all is rendered\ninto as it is; one that holds any entry, a hidden one included, is refused\nunless --overwrite is given. The outputs are then written beneath one staging\ndirectory inside it, .metais-staging, and moved into place one by one, in path\norder: a file whose path exists replaces it, by a rename that never writes into\nit or reads it, and a directory the render needs is moved in whole. Every other\nfile in the directory is left alone. Each file is whole, its old bytes or its\nnew, and a failure part way through lists the files already moved. Before\nanything is written, every output's path is checked in the directory: a symbolic\nlink or junction on it, a file where a directory must be, a name that differs\nonly in case from an existing one, a directory or a special file at it, another","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aceebda5-3671-48ae-8614-d32ad3e61363","uuid":"6d62efcd-53a5-4a42-b1b9-71cb0d7b20ae","timestamp":"2026-10-21T14:25:24.990Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/bin/bash: /etc/bash.bashrc: Permission denied\nmetais render — Render the package's outputs from the inputs supplied, into a\ndirectory or to standard output.\n\nUsage:\n  metais render <package> --out <dir|-> [supply flags] [--only <path>]\n                [--overwrite] [--dry-run] [--now <time>]\n                [--sample [--optional <mode>] [--seed <n>] [--items <n>]]\n                [--json]\n\nThe package is opened and verified whole, and the inputs are supplied and\nvalidated, as metais inspect and metais validate do; an input that fails ends\nthe render with every finding of the inputs. Then every output is planned, an\nasset or a mirror as each file it writes, its path checked by the portable-path\nrules, and rendered in memory: every output is attempted, and each reports its\nfirst error. An asset is copied as it is, never rendered: its size counts\nagainst the output limits, and its bytes are read from the package as it is\nwritten. An output declaring newline: crlf then has its line endings made CR LF,\nand one nam